    "durationMs": 403744,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified — 53/53 automated checks pass, plus a restart-persistence test.\n\n**What was built** (Rails 8 API-only, PostgreSQL via ActiveRecord):\n\n- **`POST /links`** — validates the URL (must be absolute http/https with a host), accepts an optional custom code (4–20 ASCII letters/digits/hyphens/underscores) or generates a unique 8-char one; returns `201 {\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\":0}`, `409` for duplicate codes, `422` for invalid/missing url, invalid codes, or malformed JSON\n- **`GET /links/{code}`** — `200` with link JSON, `404` JSON error when unknown\n- **`GET /r/{code}`** — `302` with `Location` exactly equal to the stored URL, atomically increments clicks once per request (`UPDATE clicks = clicks + 1`); `show`/`index` never increment\n- **`GET /links`** — `{\"items\": [...], \"total\": n}` in ascending creation order\n- **Persistence** — `links` table in Postgres (`code` unique-indexed, `clicks bigint default 0`); verified click counts and rows survive a full server restart\n\n**Two notable issues I hit and fixed:**\n\n1. The bundle resolved `json` 3.1.0, which removed the `quirks_mode` keyword that ActiveSupport 8.0's JSON encoder still passes — every `render json:` returned 500. I pinned `gem \"json\", \"~> 2.9\"` in the Gemfile.\n2. Rails eagerly consumes form-encoded bodies before the action runs, so manual body reads returned empty for requests without a JSON content-type; I switched to `request.raw_post`, which handles both cases (and also made `\"\"` codes return 422 per the \"invalid code\" rule).\n\n**Ops details:** `config/database.yml` reads only `DATABASE_URL` (no hard-coded credentials), production's `force_ssl`/`assume_ssl` are disabled for plain HTTP, and `sh start.sh` runs `db:prepare` then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` with dependencies pre-installed. Rubocop is clean, the test data has been cleared, and the server is stopped so port 8000 is free. The README explains how to start it."
  }
